  "worked_solution": "Notice that\n\n- ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ is defined for all $x$ and $y,$ and\n\n- $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061g(x,y)$ is defined if $g(x,y)$ is defined.\n\nAs a result, $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})$ is defined for all values of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the domain of $f$ is the entire $xy$-plane.",
